ISTN3MT MOBILE–CLOUD IMPLEMENTATION PROJECT Project Title: HabitTracker Module: ISTN3MT

HabitTracker is a mobile productivity app designed to help users build better routines, stay on top of daily tasks, and track personal progress over time. The app combines local mobile storage with cloud services so that it can work smoothly on-device while still supporting account-based syncing and modern smart features.

In simple terms, this project is about bringing together mobile computing, cloud computing, and emerging technologies in one practical app.

WHAT THE APP DOES (OVERVIEW)
HabitTracker allows users to:

Create and manage daily routines with timed tasks
Manage a to-do list with priorities, due dates, and recurring tasks
Write and organize personal notes
Track progress and streak analytics
Sign in securely and sync selected data with cloud services
Use an AI assistant to generate routines from goals
Receive a daily smart briefing using location + weather + quote APIs
This gives the app both strong core functionality (CRUD and tracking) and innovation features (AI + context-aware content).

CRUD REQUIREMENTS (READ, INSERT, EDIT, DELETE)
The app fully supports CRUD operations. The easiest place to demonstrate this in class is the To-Do feature:

CREATE (Insert data):

User taps + and adds a new to-do item
Example for demo: Title = Ashley, Description = ashley@ukzn.ac.za
READ (Read data):

User views to-do lists (active/overdue/completed)
Can filter by category and sort by priority/date
UPDATE (Edit data):

User opens the Ashley item and edits details
Example: change description/email to ashley.m@ukzn.ac.za
DELETE (Delete data):

User deletes the Ashley item
Item is removed from the list
CRUD is also present in routines and notes, but To-Do is the quickest for marking.

MOBILE SYSTEMS (HW + SW)
MOBILE HARDWARE CONTEXT: The app runs on standard smartphone hardware, including:

SoC (CPU/GPU): handles app logic, UI rendering, and background tasks
Memory (RAM): stores runtime state and app processes
Storage (flash): stores local app database
Sensors/services: location service is used for daily weather briefing
User equipment: Android phone/tablet
Transmission: Wi-Fi/mobile data for cloud and API communication
MOBILE SOFTWARE CONTEXT:

Android OS (Linux kernel based)
App built in Kotlin
Jetpack Compose + Material 3 for UI
Coroutines and StateFlow for reactive behavior
Hilt for dependency injection
Room (SQLite) for local data persistence
APPLICATION LAYER (UI, NETWORKING, DATA, SECURITY, CLOUD)
UI Design & Components:

Built with Jetpack Compose and Material 3
Includes auth, dashboard, to-do, notes, analytics, profile, and AI screens
UI is reactive and updates automatically from ViewModel state
Networking & API Integration:

Uses Retrofit + OkHttp for HTTP communication
Integrates weather, quote, reverse-geocoding, and AI services
Data Persistence & Storage:

Local: Room + SQLite (offline-friendly structured storage)
Cloud: Firebase Firestore (NoSQL real-time cloud storage)
Security & Authentication:

Firebase Authentication
Email/password login and Google sign-in
Session-based access to user-specific cloud data
HTTPS for secure transport
Backend Services & Cloud Integration:

Firebase services running on Google Cloud infrastructure
Cloud Firestore used for synced user data
Authentication and real-time data observation included
NETWORKING & COMMUNICATION
The app communicates over internet channels using mobile/Wi-Fi connectivity:

Short/medium/long range communication is handled by typical mobile network infrastructure
API calls use secure HTTPS
Firestore provides managed real-time sync behavior
The app demonstrates practical mobile-to-cloud communication flow
SECURITY
Security in this project is addressed through:

Authenticated user access (Firebase Auth)
User-scoped cloud data organization
Runtime permission handling for location
Secure API communication over HTTPS
Controlled app behavior when permissions are denied (fallback logic)
EMERGING TECHNOLOGIES IN THIS PROJECT
This project includes modern/emerging elements:

Generative AI feature (AI Routine Architect using Gemini API)
Context-aware mobile feature (location-based daily briefing)
Hybrid architecture (local SQL + cloud NoSQL)
Real-time cloud observation (snapshot listeners)
These features enhance user experience and demonstrate current industry trends beyond basic CRUD apps.

CLOUD COMPONENTS (HW + SW VIEW)
CLOUD HARDWARE VIEW (conceptual):

Uses distributed cloud infrastructure (clusters/nodes managed by provider)
Scalable backend services without manually managing servers
CLOUD SOFTWARE VIEW:

Managed services: Firebase Authentication + Firestore
API service layer for external data sources
Mix of open-source libraries (Retrofit/Room) and proprietary cloud platforms (Firebase/Gemini endpoints)
LIVE DEMO FLOW (MATCHING PRESENTATION PROTOCOL)
Recommended demo sequence for marking:

Sign in to show cloud-enabled session
Go to To-Do and perform full CRUD:
Create Ashley record
Read/find the record
Update email field
Delete record
Show one enhanced feature:
AI routine generation OR Daily briefing card
Briefly show dashboard analytics/progress
Tip: narrate each step slowly and clearly while you perform it.

PROJECT VALUE
HabitTracker is not just a checklist app — it is a full mobile-cloud solution that demonstrates:

Clean architecture design
Complete CRUD lifecycle
Local + cloud data strategy
Authentication and security
Real API integration
AI-assisted user experience
